\
     Actually wait - let me think more carefully. The\
     network takes a shuffled image as input. The\
     output is (16, 4, 4). Each spatial position (h,w)\
      in the 4x4 output corresponds to a region in the\
      shuffled image. The target Y = gt_label gets\
     reshaped to (4,4). So Y_hw[h,w] =\
     gt_label[h*4+w].\
\
     gt_label[original_id] = new_pos. So Y_hw[h,w] =\
     gt_label[h*4+w] where h*4+w is treated as an\
     original_id. This means at spatial position\
     (h,w), the target is "where did original patch\
     h*4+w end up in the shuffled image?"\
\
     But spatial position (h,w) in the output doesn't\
     correspond to original patch h*4+w - it\
     corresponds to the shuffled patch at that\
     position!\
\
     This is the training convention that was\
     established. The accuracy metric compares pred[i]\
      == gt[i] using the same convention. So the model\
      learns this mapping internally, and it's\
     consistent.\
